Section: 3.1 Encoding with LSTM and Gated CNN
Text: 3.1 Encoding with LSTM and Gated CNN In this method, paragraphs are encoded separately, and the concatenation of the resulted encoding is going through the classiﬁer. First, each paragraph is encoded with LSTM. The hidden state at the end of each sentence is extracted, and the resulting matrix is going through gated CNN (Dauphin et al., 2017) for extraction of single encoding for each paragraph.

